/-!
# The ambient regular locus along a J-2 closed fibre

Source: Kurano--Shimomoto, Ideal-adic completion of quasi-excellent rings (after Gabber),
Lemma 4.2 and Claim 4.3, printed pp. 4--5; J-2 as in Stacks Project, Tag 07P7
(blueprint: lem-per-j2-closed-fibre-regular-locus).
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

/-- The ambient regular locus restricted to the closed fibre over `V(I)` is open there;
its complement in that fibre is closed in the ambient scheme.

Source: Kurano--Shimomoto, Lemma 4.2 and Claim 4.3, printed pp. 4--5
(blueprint: lem-per-j2-closed-fibre-regular-locus).

Proof:
1. On a finite affine cover write `U = Spec B`, where `B` is finite type over `A`.
   By `lem-weil-pbc-finite-type-algebra-noetherian`, both `B` and `C = B/IB` are
   Noetherian. The quotient-spectrum homeomorphism identifies the closed fibre on
   this chart with `Spec C`, and `lem-weil-pbc-affine-open-stalk-localization`
   identifies the ambient stalks with `B_p`. It suffices to show that the primes
   in `V(IB)` for which `B_p` is regular local form a relatively open subset `E`.
2. Regularity is stable under generalization: if `p` is contained in `q`, then
   `B_p` is a prime localization of `B_q`, by `lem-weil-pbc-primes-of-localization`
   and `lem-weil-pbc-localize-localization-at-prime`. Apply
   `lem-weil-pbc-regular-local-localization`.
3. Every nonempty irreducible closed subset of `V(IB)` is `V(q)` for a prime
   containing `IB`, by `lem-weil-pbc-spec-irreducible-closed-subsets-primes` and
   the quotient-spectrum homeomorphism. If `B_q` is not regular, step 2 shows that
   `V(q)` is disjoint from `E`.
4. Otherwise `B/q` is a finite type `A/I`-algebra. The J-2 hypothesis makes its
   regular locus open. It contains the generic point, whose local ring is its
   fraction field, hence regular of dimension zero. The basic-open basis gives
   `b` outside `q` such that `(B/q)_(p/q)` is regular whenever `p` contains `q`
   and avoids `b` (`lem-weil-pbc-spec-localization-away-basic-open`).
5. Choose `d = dim B_q` generators of its maximal ideal. Write them as fractions
   `a_i/s_i` and replace them by their unit multiples `a_i/1`, with `a_i` in `q`.
   By `lem-weil-pbc-regular-local-generators-regular-sequence` these form a regular
   sequence. By `lem-exc-regular-sequence-principal-neighbourhood`, it is regular
   in `B_g` for some `g` outside `q`, also when the sequence is empty.
6. Let `K` be the ideal generated by the `a_i`. Choose finitely many generators
   `t_j` of `q`. Since `K B_q = q B_q`, denominator clearing
   (`lem-exc-localization-ideal-membership-clearing`) gives `s_j` outside `q`
   with `s_j t_j` in `K`. Their product `s` is outside `q` and satisfies `s q ⊆ K`.
   Hence `K B_p = q B_p` when `p` avoids `s`. An empty product is `1`.
7. Set `h = b*g*s`. For `p` containing `q` and avoiding `h`, the sequence of the
   `a_i/1` in `B_p` is weakly regular by
   `lem-exc-weakly-regular-sequence-localization`. Its final quotient is nonzero
   since every `a_i` lies in `p`, so it is regular. Step 6 and
   `lem-weil-pbc-localization-at-prime-of-quotient` identify its quotient with
   `(B/q)_(p/q)`, regular by step 4. The ring `B_p` is Noetherian and local;
   `lem-exc-regular-local-lift-regular-sequence-quotient` makes it regular.
   Thus `V(q) ∩ D(h)` is a nonempty relatively open subset contained in `E`.
8. Steps 3 and 7 apply the criterion
   `lem-trf-noetherian-constructible-subset-criterion` on `Spec C`, making `E`
   constructible there. Step 2 gives generalization stability in `Spec C`.
   Apply `lem-trf-spectrum-constructible-generalization-open` and transport
   through the quotient-spectrum homeomorphism to obtain openness on the chart.
9. The chartwise opens glue to an open in the subspace `f⁻¹V(I)`. Its complement
   is closed in that subspace. The subspace is closed in `X`, since `V(I)` is
   closed and `f` is continuous. Hence the complement is closed in `X` as well.
   Conversely ambient closedness gives the same relative openness.
-/
theorem isOpen_regularLocus_on_j2_closedFibre
    (A : Type u) [CommRing A] [IsNoetherianRing A] (I : Ideal A)
    (X : Scheme.{u}) (f : X ⟶ Spec (CommRingCat.of A))
    [LocallyOfFiniteType f] [QuasiCompact f]
    (hJ : ∀ (B : Type u) [CommRing B] [Algebra (A ⧸ I) B]
      [Algebra.FiniteType (A ⧸ I) B],
      IsOpen {p : PrimeSpectrum B |
        IsRegularLocalRing (Localization.AtPrime p.asIdeal)}) :
    IsOpen {x : {x : X // f x ∈ PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (I : Set A)} |
      IsRegularLocalRing (X.presheaf.stalk x.1)} ∧
    IsClosed {x : X | f x ∈ PrimeSpectrum.zeroLocus (I : Set A) ∧
      ¬ IsRegularLocalRing (X.presheaf.stalk x)} := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry
